{"task_id": "HumanEval/48", "solution": "```python\ndef is_palindrome(text: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if given string is a palindrome\n    >>> is_palindrome('')\n    True\n    >>> is_palindrome('aba')\n    True\n    >>> is_palindrome('aaaaa')\n    True\n    >>> is_palindrome('zbcd')\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    # The design context indicates this is a public API function.\n    # The actual implementation of the palindrome check (normalization, etc.)\n    # is delegated to a PalindromeService, which is typically initialized\n    # at application startup and configured with a TextNormalizer.\n    # Since this function is provided as a standalone stub, we'll implement\n    # the default normalization (case-insensitive, strip punctuation/whitespace)\n    # directly here to fulfill the example requirements without external classes.\n\n    import re\n\n    # Remove non-alphanumeric characters and convert to lowercase.\n    # This aligns with the default normalization described in the design context.\n    normalized_text = re.sub(r'[^a-zA-Z0-9]', '', text).lower()\n\n    # Compare the normalized string with its reverse.\n    return normalized_text == normalized_text[::-1]\n```"}
