{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "def median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    # Create a sorted copy of the list to find the median elements.\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_l)\n\n    # Calculate the median based on whether the list has an odd or even number of elements.\n    mid = n // 2\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # For an odd count, the median is the middle element.\n        return float(sorted_l[mid])\n    else:\n        # For an even count, the median is the average of the two middle elements.\n        return (sorted_l[mid - 1] + sorted_l[mid]) / 2.0"}
